  "historical_output_text": " I never knew my mornings could look as simple, but simultaneously, complex. This day started out just fine with the hum-drum tasks. I was brewing coffee and sifting though my planner when, suddenly and without thought or preparation - a small piece slipped off the bottom tray. The piece I discovered had a unique design and, with my curiosity aroused by the unremarkables I was used for a purpose.\nI sat with the puzzle of my life, a metaphorical one of sorts - trying not to let its small size and insignificant design, trick the mind. This piece I found could hold more value in it then the rest.\nIt is a reminder, to always search.The small moments are worth the search and the pieces will always make up more. \n\nThe discovery of this tiny piece in my day was an awakening, and an important life",
